subject: fix(memory): contextCompactor sequence validity — tool-pair boundary + no synthetic ack

PR #3599 review §3 reproduced two defects:
1. keep=2 with trailing tool result left a dangling tool message whose
   tool_call_id had no matching tool_calls in the kept window (tc14).
2. The synthetic assistant ack inserted after the summary created an
   assistant->assistant alternation break when the first kept message was
   an assistant message.

Fixes:
- Walk the cut back to a tool_use/tool_result pair boundary so pairs stay
  together (no dangling tool results).
- Drop the synthetic assistant ack entirely; merge the summary into the
  first kept user message when it is a user message (no user->user
  adjacency either).
- Add validateSequence() (no same-role adjacency for user/assistant, no
  dangling tool results, unresolved tool_calls tracked) and skip
  compaction for the round when the resulting sequence is invalid.

Tests: added 11 context-compactor regression tests covering keep 2/3/4
with a trailing tool result, assistant-first recent window, summary merge,
validator behavior, input-array form; extended tests/unit/
memory-enhancements.test.js. 14/14 pass via node --test.

